    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "The Everyday Pattern",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The most common everyday pattern is definite noun plus possessive. Definite means the noun has definite meaning, as in the car or the house."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Use a definite noun first, then the possessive: "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "bilen min",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "huset mitt",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "bøkene mine",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Bilen min er blå."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "My car is blue."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Veska mi er her."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "My bag is here."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Huset mitt er lite."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "My house is small."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Bøkene mine ligger på bordet."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "My books are on the table."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "contrast",
      "title": "Possessive Before the Noun",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Norwegian can also put the possessive before the noun. Then the noun is indefinite, so it does not have definite meaning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Before the noun, use possessive plus indefinite noun: "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "min bil",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "mitt hus",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "mine bøker",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Min bil er blå."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "My car is blue."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Mitt hus er lite."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "My house is small."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "tip",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "The after-noun pattern is very common in normal speech. The before-noun pattern is also correct, and it can sound a little more focused or formal."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
